7873: # (wave 26b, D10, D12) Waits for an engine turn's process: its wall-clock limit ($TimeoutSec), the
7874: # stall cut ($StallSec > 0: no complete event line appended to $EventsPath for that long while the
7875: # process lives - the codex --json items, agy's stream-json, muse's MSP records all go to that
7876: # file line by line; the clock starts with the turn) and the operator's kick ($KickPath appears).
7877: # Polls every second (TEST HOOK: CODEX_CONSULT_TEST_WAIT_TICK_MS). Kills nothing - the caller
7878: # stops the tree. { Exited; Reason ('' | 'timeout' | 'stall' | 'kick'); Events (lines seen);
7879: # LastEvent (DateTimeOffset of the last line seen, $null when none); Silent (seconds without an
7880: # event at the stall cut) }.
7881: function Wait-EngineProcess {
7882:     param($Process, [int]$TimeoutSec, [int]$StallSec = 0, [string]$EventsPath = '', [string]$KickPath = '')
